/P 82 0 R
/E (I took part in a safety-focused engineering project developed to evaluate a patented energy-absorbing system mounted at the rear of truck trailers in order to reduce driver fatalities in rear-end collisions. Since the test vehicle did not contain a driver, we developed a dedicated control system for steering and a release mechanism to enable the vehicle to be guided and deployed safely during impact testing. As a member of the project team, I contributed to the development of this test setup, which supported the practical evaluation of the trailer rear-impact safety system under controlled conditions. This project strengthened my experience in mechanical system development, test engineering, and safety-oriented design.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
